// Batch 003: restates the curated name of every race batches 001 and
// 002 curate, for a database that already holds those batches.
//
// A source importer names a race only when it creates the row, so a
// long-lived database can still carry a source's spelling for a row whose
// curated name came later -- TP's "Gyttjevrålarna FC" for the team curated as
// "Gyttjevrålarna", BBL's "Bretonnians" for the race curated as "Bretonnian".
// Batches are applied once and never re-applied, so this batch restates every
// curated name a single time and leaves each row on the name a fresh import
// ends with. On a fresh import it changes nothing.
//
// Each entry carries only `name` and `externalIds`. The name is the one the
// last batch 001/002 entry sharing an external id with the row gives it (the
// after phase runs last, and files run in alphabetical order); the external
// ids are every id those entries declare. curated-data-batch-003.spec.ts
// enforces both, so this file cannot drift from the batches it restates.
{
  externalSystems: [
    { name: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', category: 'imported_data_source' },
    { name: 'tourplay.net', category: 'imported_data_source' },
  ],
  races: [
    { name: 'Amazon', externalIds: [{ system: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', id: '1' }, { system: 'tourplay.net', id: 'Amazon_BB2020' }] },
    { name: 'Black Orc', externalIds: [{ system: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', id: '44' }, { system: 'tourplay.net', id: 'BlackOrc' }] },
